<http://data.silknow.org/object/b3cbf372-16bd-38fd-a3a6-2c1fbb562512/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Women saved their most elaborate dresses for special occasions such as balls. Lavish gowns embellished with gold thread or sparkling beads glittered in the artificial light of the dancing room. Thin, gauzy materials created a soft dreamy look. These light materials also prevented the wearer from getting too hot while dancing in stuffy, overcrowded spaces."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/b3cbf372-16bd-38fd-a3a6-2c1fbb562512> .

